MCPJam Inspector on Railway — deployment packaging
===================================================

This repository is a **Railway deployment mirror** of MCPJam Inspector, a
community-contributed packaging. It vendors the upstream source tree verbatim
at a pinned commit so that the Railway build is reproducible, and adds nothing
to the application itself.

Upstream project
----------------

*   Name: **MCPJam Inspector** (`@mcpjam/inspector`), by MCPJam
*   Website: https://www.mcpjam.com
*   Source: https://github.com/MCPJam/inspector
*   Docs: https://docs.mcpjam.com
*   License: Apache License 2.0 — see `LICENSE` (upstream's, unmodified)

The vendored commit is recorded in `UPSTREAM_COMMIT`.

What was changed relative to upstream
-------------------------------------

Only packaging and documentation. No application code, no build definition and
no dependency was modified.

*   `mcpjam-inspector/Dockerfile` — unmodified, upstream's own multi-stage
    image build. Upstream ships a `railway.json` that points Railway at this
    exact file, so the image Railway builds here is byte-for-byte the image
    upstream documents for `docker build -f mcpjam-inspector/Dockerfile .`.
*   `railway.json` — unmodified, upstream's.
*   `.dockerignore` — added. Every excluded path is not copied by any stage of
    the Dockerfile, so the built image is unchanged; it only trims ~35 MB of
    documentation screenshots and GitHub automation from the build context.
*   `README.md` — replaced. The deployment guide for this repository. The
    upstream README is preserved verbatim as `UPSTREAM_README.md`.
*   `NOTICE`, `UPSTREAM_COMMIT` — added (attribution and pin).
*   `assets/` — four screenshots from the upstream documentation, used by the
    README. Screenshots are the property of their authors; they are reused from
    the upstream repository under its Apache 2.0 license and are not modified.
*   Removed, because they are not needed to build or run the image and are not
    part of the product: `.github/workflows/` (upstream CI, which requires
    MCPJam's own secrets), `.github/scripts/`, `.github/rulesets/`,
    `.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/`, `.github/dependabot.yml`,
    `.github/FUNDING.yml`, `docs/` (kept only the four screenshots above),
    `examples/`, `notes/`, `ops/`, `actions/`, `skills/`, `design-explorations/`,
    `preview-router/`, `.release-plan/`, `.spike-codex-appserver/`,
    `.changeset/`, `NOTES-item-2.md`, `NOTES-item-3.md`.

Apache 2.0 compliance
---------------------

The upstream `LICENSE` is retained unmodified at the root of this repository,
as §4(a) requires. This file and `README.md` carry the attribution that §4(b)
requires. The vendored source is unmodified, so no source-change notice is
required.

